    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        40,
        420
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        600
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "How to use (Anima)\n\nAnima is not a checkpoint. It loads as three files: Load Diffusion Model (anima-turbo-v1.1 or anima-base-v1.0), Load CLIP (qwen_3_06b_base, type stable_diffusion) and Load VAE (qwen_image_vae).\n\n1. While exploring prompts, select the hires-pass nodes (ImageScaleBy through Save Image) and press Ctrl+B to bypass them. You then only get the fast base preview (about 20 s).\n2. When you like an image, set the base KSampler seed to fixed, un-bypass the hires nodes and run once more.\n\nTurbo settings (all three samplers): cfg 1.0, euler, simple. Base 10 steps, hires and detailers 10 steps.\nAt cfg 1.0 the negative prompt is skipped. Describe what you want in the positive instead.\nBase model: switch Load Diffusion Model to anima-base-v1.0 and use steps 30, cfg 4.0, er_sde, simple in all samplers (the detailers 20 steps). The negative prompt then works. It is 3 to 4 times slower.\n\nPrompts: quality tags first (masterpiece, best quality, score_7, safe), then Danbooru tags, then plain sentences. Artist tags take an @ prefix, for example @artist name.\n\nLoRA: only Anima LoRAs work, not SDXL or Illustrious ones. To use more than one, add another Load LoRA node and chain it (MODEL and CLIP out of the first into the second). Bypass with Ctrl+B to render without it.\n\nHires pass: denoise 0.35 to 0.45 adds detail. Higher values start changing the picture.\nFace detailer: redraws the face at guide_size 768, denoise 0.45. Hand detailer: guide_size 512, denoise 0.4. Bypass either with Ctrl+B.\nAnime Post FX: set any effect to 0 to turn it off."
      ]
    },
